description:
## What

Extend `pkix-path::ValidationPolicy` with two new leaf-only predicate fields and the enforcement code in `chain_walk`. Unblocks per-tier S/MIME profile differentiation in `pkix-profiles-cabf` (PKIX-jbvb.1 / .2 / .3).

## Design (locked by Mark 2026-05-13 on PKIX-jbvb parent)

### New fields on `ValidationPolicy`

```rust
/// If `Some(oids)`, the leaf certificate must explicitly assert every OID in
/// `oids` via its `CertificatePolicies` extension. `None` means no policy-OID
/// requirement (the default).
///
/// Distinct from [`initial_policy_set`][Self::initial_policy_set]:
/// `initial_policy_set` is the relying party's *acceptable* policy set (RFC 5280
/// §6.1.1, `user-initial-policy-set`). `required_leaf_policy_oids` requires
/// *assertion* — the OID must appear on the leaf cert.
///
/// `anyPolicy` (2.5.29.32.0) does **not** satisfy a specific OID check.
/// Violations produce [`Error::MissingLeafPolicyOid`].
pub required_leaf_policy_oids: Option<Vec<ObjectIdentifier>>,

/// If `Some(rule)`, the leaf certificate's Subject DN must match `rule`.
/// `None` means no Subject DN requirement (the default).
///
/// Violations produce [`Error::SubjectDnAttrRuleUnmet`].
pub required_leaf_subject_dn_attrs: Option<DnAttrRule>,
```

### New expression type

```rust
/// Compositional rule for asserting required Subject DN attributes on a leaf cert.
///
/// Designed to express CA/B Forum S/MIME BR tier rules like
/// "must have organizationName" or "must have pseudonym OR (givenName AND surname)".
///
/// The `Field` variant matches when the named OID appears at least once in the
/// leaf's Subject DN RDN sequence. `AllOf` and `AnyOf` compose subordinate rules.
/// `AnyOf([])` is vacuously false; `AllOf([])` is vacuously true.
#[non_exhaustive]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[cfg_attr(feature = "serde", derive(serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize))]
pub enum DnAttrRule {
    Field(ObjectIdentifier),
    AllOf(Vec<DnAttrRule>),
    AnyOf(Vec<DnAttrRule>),
}
```

### Enforcement

Leaf-only check sites in `chain_walk`, adjacent to the existing `required_leaf_eku` block. Both new fields are additive under `#[non_exhaustive]` (no API break).

### New `Error` variants

Both are leaf-only diagnostic errors. Added to the existing `#[non_exhaustive]` enum, so additive.

```rust
/// The leaf certificate's CertificatePolicies extension does not assert a
/// required policy OID (from [`ValidationPolicy::required_leaf_policy_oids`]).
MissingLeafPolicyOid { required: ObjectIdentifier },

/// The leaf certificate's Subject DN does not satisfy
/// [`ValidationPolicy::required_leaf_subject_dn_attrs`].
SubjectDnAttrRuleUnmet,
```

The `SubjectDnAttrRuleUnmet` variant carries no payload at v0.x. Richer "which branch of the rule failed" diagnostics are a non-breaking follow-up; the variant struct is `#[non_exhaustive]` from the start (workspace convention).

## Acceptance

- [ ] `DnAttrRule` enum lives in `pkix-path` alongside `ValidationPolicy`. Public, `#[non_exhaustive]`, derives `Clone + Debug + PartialEq + Eq` + serde cfg-gate.
- [ ] `ValidationPolicy` gains `required_leaf_policy_oids` + `required_leaf_subject_dn_attrs` fields with Default = None.
- [ ] `chain_walk` enforces both fields at the leaf, only when `Some`. Disabled (None) path identical to today.
- [ ] Two new `Error` variants. Both carry leaf-cert-position info via the existing diagnostic pattern.
- [ ] Unit tests:
  - Positive: leaf asserts required OID → pass; leaf has required DN attr → pass.
  - Negative: leaf missing OID → `MissingLeafPolicyOid`; leaf missing all branches of `AllOf` → `SubjectDnAttrRuleUnmet`.
  - Composition: `AnyOf([Field(pseudonym), AllOf([Field(givenName), Field(surname)])])` matches a leaf with pseudonym only; matches a leaf with givenName + surname; rejects a leaf with neither.
  - Vacuity: `AllOf(vec![])` accepts everything; `AnyOf(vec![])` rejects everything (cite in rustdoc).
- [ ] Test fixtures use existing committed cert fixtures from `pkix-path/tests/fixtures/`; no new openssl-generated certs unless an existing fixture cannot exercise the new fields.
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry in `pkix-path`.
- [ ] Rustdoc for both new fields cross-references the existing `required_leaf_eku` precedent and the BR-tier-disambiguation use case.

## Out of scope

- Per-tier `Profile::policy()` impls — those are PKIX-jbvb.{1,2,3}.
- "Which branch of the AllOf failed" detailed diagnostics — non-breaking follow-up if useful.
- `OneOf` (XOR) variant — file follow-up if a tier needs it.
- Wiring this into `BasicSmimeProfile` (pkix-profiles RFC-baseline) — RFC 8551 doesn't require any of this. Only `-cabf` consumers populate the new fields.

